Task: Migrate inventory-service to PureConfig (Phase 2, observability-config_20260927)

Summary: inventory-service previously read port/metrics-port/induced-failure defaults via
raw sys.env.get(...) calls in Main.scala, unlike order-service's PureConfig-based
approach. Added pureconfig-core to inventory-service's build.sbt, created
InventoryServiceConfig (port, metricsPort, serviceName, inducedFailure: InducedFailureConfig,
derives ConfigReader, load[F]) and a new application.conf, matching order-service's
default + ${?ENV_VAR}-override convention. Kept all existing env var names unchanged
(INVENTORY_SERVICE_PORT, INVENTORY_SERVICE_METRICS_PORT, INVENTORY_INDUCED_FAILURE_RATE,
INVENTORY_INDUCED_DELAY_MS) plus a new INVENTORY_SERVICE_NAME. Main.scala now loads
config once and uses config.serviceName at all 3 Tracing/Metrics/Logging call sites,
replacing the hardcoded "inventory-service" literal. Confirmed Typesafe Config's
duration parsing treats a bare numeric override (e.g. INVENTORY_INDUCED_DELAY_MS=500) as
milliseconds by default, preserving the old sys.env contract exactly.

TDD: wrote InventoryServiceConfigSuite first (Red — pureconfig not on the classpath yet,
InventoryServiceConfig didn't exist), then implemented (Green).

Full repo test suite: 45+23+29 = 97 passed, 0 failed (three separate sbt test-summary
batches). scalafmt caught real formatting issues in both order-service's and
inventory-service's Main.scala after edits — fixed via sbt scalafmt before this commit.

